  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, minimal baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the design space: it uses the least complex RNA encoder (PCA), a single profile (no aggregation needed), and no image or fusion components. This isolates the fundamental RNA signal quality without confounding from learned encoders, multi-profile aggregation, or cross-modal fusion. It will tell us the performance floor for RNA alone, which is essential context for interpreting whether richer encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or multimodal fusion actually add value. Starting from this null model ensures that every later experiment can be interpreted as a controlled addition of one design axis, maximizing the information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

